@page "/guide"

<PageTitle>BlokeBot user guide</PageTitle>

<article class="article-shell article-shell--wide guide-home">
    <header class="article-header article-header--split">
        <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">User guide</p>
            <h1>Do the next useful thing.</h1>
        </div>
        <p class="lede">These guides follow BlokeBot's navigation and use the words shown in the dashboard. Start with your current task rather than reading from the beginning.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="guide-launch" aria-labelledby="guide-start-heading">
        <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">New channel</p>
            <h2 id="guide-start-heading">From Twitch sign-in to a ready bot</h2>
            <p>Choose the correct account, select a channel, complete both Twitch connections and start the bot only after readiness is green.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="button button-primary" href="guide/getting-started"><SiteIcon Name="book" />Start here</a>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="guide-topics-heading">
        <div class="section-intro">
            <p class="eyebrow">Task index</p>
            <h2 id="guide-topics-heading">Find the screen you are using</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="guide-grid guide-grid--numbered">
            @foreach (var topic in SiteGuideCatalog.All.Skip(1).Select((topic, index) => (Topic: topic, Index: index + 1)))
            {
                <article class="guide-card">
                    <span class="guide-card__number">@topic.Index.ToString("00")</span>
                    <p class="eyebrow">@topic.Topic.Eyebrow</p>
                    <h3><a href="@topic.Topic.Href">@topic.Topic.Title</a></h3>
                    <p>@topic.Topic.Summary</p>
                    <a class="guide-card__arrow" href="@topic.Topic.Href" aria-label="Open @topic.Topic.Title"><SiteIcon Name="arrow" /></a>
                </article>
            }
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="help-grid" aria-labelledby="help-heading">
        <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">When something is wrong</p>
            <h2 id="help-heading">Start with the visible state</h2>
            <p>Check the selected channel, Alerts and Bot status before reconnecting accounts. The troubleshooting guide explains what information is safe and useful to send to the server owner.</p>
            <a class="text-link" href="troubleshooting">Troubleshoot BlokeBot</a>
        </div>
        <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Technical operations</p>
            <h2>Installing or hosting?</h2>
            <p>Server setup has its own path for Twitch developer credentials, callback URLs, HTTPS, process state and backups.</p>
            <a class="text-link" href="server-owners">Open server setup</a>
        </div>
    </section>
</article>
